<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1992/19/eng@/~cl_12> <https://schema.org/text> "entertainment licence or a licence to open an entertainmenl place under this Act is refused, or a holder of a licence which is revoked, or any person aggrieved by the imposition of any conditions or restrictions on or subject to which a licence is granted or any person who is aggrieved by the forfeiture of security under section 10, may, within thirty days after being informed in writing of the refusal, or revocation, or the imposition of the conditions or restrictions, or forfeiture, as the case may be, appeal against such decision to the Minister, who shall confirm or set aside the decision; and the decision of the Minister shall be final and shall not be questioned in any court."@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1992/19/eng@> .
